 [17592186420906 1077 "selection" 13194139534420 17592186045417 true] [17592186420906 1078 #edb/ref 17592186420873 13194139534420 17592186045417 true] [17592186420906 1079 #uuid "e4055bff-eb04-5d8c-8a7f-fd7faf3e0c1d" 13194139534420 17592186045417 true] [17592186420907 1075 #edb/ref 17592186420875 13194139534420 17592186045417 true] [17592186420907 1075 #edb/ref 17592186420876 13194139534420 17592186045417 true] [17592186420907 1075 #edb/ref 17592186420885 13194139534420 17592186045417 true] [17592186420907 1075 #edb/ref 17592186420888 13194139534420 17592186045417 true] [17592186420907 1075 #edb/ref 17592186420892 13194139534420 17592186045417 true] [17592186420907 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534420 17592186045417 true] [17592186420907 1077 "selection" 13194139534420 17592186045417 true] [17592186420907 1078 #edb/ref 17592186420888 13194139534420 17592186045417 true] [17592186420907 1079 #uuid "e89aabf0-d356-583a-a3cf-404273cddd70" 13194139534420 17592186045417 true] [17592186420908 1075 #edb/ref 17592186420867 13194139534420 17592186045417 true] [17592186420908 1075 #edb/ref 17592186420878 13194139534420 17592186045417 true] [17592186420908 1075 #edb/ref 17592186420893 13194139534420 17592186045417 true] [17592186420908 1075 #edb/ref 17592186420895 13194139534420 17592186045417 true] [17592186420908 1075 #edb/ref 17592186420898 13194139534420 17592186045417 true] [17592186420908 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534420 17592186045417 true] [17592186420908 1077 "selection" 13194139534420 17592186045417 true] [17592186420908 1078 #edb/ref 17592186420893 13194139534420 17592186045417 true] [17592186420908 1079 #uuid "fd37f018-666a-5dbb-8a05-7813cb84c875" 13194139534420 17592186045417 true] [17592186420909 1068 #edb/ref 17592186420906 13194139534420 17592186045417 true] [17592186420909 1069 "q-127058" 13194139534420 17592186045417 true] [17592186420909 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534420 17592186045417 true] [17592186420909 1071 "![](images/65/653699a9c78577272425de7f8e6d015743e2c2e8c6e9a21bef189dc06fd80684.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F(x,y)={x}^{5}{y}^{7}\\,i+x{y}^{3}\\,j$ and the rectangle $C$ shown above. If the flux of $F$ across the side ${C}_{1}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{1}}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}s,\n$$\n\nwhat is the missing expression?" 13194139534420 17592186045417 true] [17592186420909 1072 #uuid "07e888b6-1046-5ef1-87ef-0610d3939941" 13194139534420 17592186045417 true] [17592186420909 1074 "If $F$ is a vector field and $C$ is a piecewise-smooth, simple, closed curve, then the flux of $F$ across $C$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ denotes the outward-pointing unit normal vector to $C.$\n\nIn our case, we need to find an expression for the flux across only the part ${C}_{1}$ of the closed curve $C.$ Since this side is perpendicular to the $x$-axis and we require an outward-pointing unit normal vector, we must have $n=i.$\n\n![](images/35/35e33731fbe85305a4308ef03c9f793b77558d66350d9345c30e643df1c40ba1.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}({x}^{5}{y}^{7}\\,i+x{y}^{3}\\,j)\\cdot i\\,\\text{d}s \\\\  & ={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}{x}^{5}{y}^{7}\\,\\text{d}s\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing expression is ${x}^{5}{y}^{7}.$" 13194139534420 17592186045417 true] [17592186420910 1068 #edb/ref 17592186420902 13194139534420 17592186045417 true] [17592186420910 1069 "q-127026" 13194139534420 17592186045417 true] [17592186420910 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534420 17592186045417 true] [17592186420910 1071 "![](images/28/28a7eb32cfcd800c907e9f4af927eca7bd8616d36162682413db62a9feabefbb.png)\n\nConsider the ellipse $S$ and vector field $F$ shown above. Let $C$ be any path where $S$ is traversed once in the clockwise direction. \n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- The flux of $F$ across $C$ is negative\n- The flux of $F$ across $C$ is zero\n- The flux of $F$ across $-C$ is positive" 13194139534420 17592186045417 true] [17592186420910 1072 #uuid "0ae03bac-e2a8-5c3b-a5da-8c8f23590a03" 13194139534420 17592186045417 true] [17592186420910 1074 "If $F$ is a vector field and $C$ is a piecewise-smooth, simple, closed curve, then the flux of $F$ across $C$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ denotes the outward-pointing unit normal vector to $C.$\n\nTo understand the flux intuitively, we imagine that $F$ represents a stream of flowing water. The flux of $F$ across $C$ represents the net flow of water escaping the region bounded by $C:$ \n\n- If more water flows out through $C$ than in through $C$ (i.e., there is a net flow *out* through $C$), the flux is *positive*.\n\n- If more water flows in through $C$ than out through $C$ (i.e., there is a net flow *in* through $C$), the flux is *negative*.\n\n![](images/a7/a72dc9866562a42a49590fd169424307675b2c14b36833bd729026f46b677eec.png)\n\n- If the net flow through $C$ is zero then the flux equals zero.\n\n![](images/3a/3a6ac8656b2e0b5cc482a16eb3a4fab57cb681c9a40cf634da47f9a4323d9fdf.png)\n\nFor an arbitrary closed curve, the outward-pointing unit normal vector tells us which direction is \"out.\"\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statements I and II are false. From the diagram below it's clear that there is a net flow *out* through $C.$ \n\n![](images/fe/fecf59674259d41222ffd981b1ab6d90c474fe2b0e37a6d5f7626f34536a6896.png)\n\nTherefore, the flux is positive, and we must have\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s>0.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. When measuring flux through a closed curve, the orientation of the curve does not matter because the outward-pointing unit normal vector is the same at each point on $C$ in either case.\n\n![](images/56/56a7fc09ed2a2a15b0949fa6041dc9c0ee6beb69f30b1a5c048afd8c57887d52.png)\n\nSo, the flux of $F$ across $-C$ is positive, and we must have\n\n$$\n{∮}_{-C}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s>0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer